.TH FLOOR 3
.SH NAME
floor, ceil, fabs, fmod \- floor, ceiling, absolute value, remainder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <math.h>

double
floor(x)
double x;

double
ceil(x)
double x;

double
fabs(x)
double x;

double
fmod(x, y)
double x, y;
.fi
.PP
cc ... \-lm
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B floor
returns the largest whole number not greater than
.IR x ,
and
.B ceil
the smallest whole number not less than
.IR x .
.PP
.B fabs
returns the absolute value of
.IR x .
.PP
.B fmod
returns the remainder of
.I x
divided by
.IR y :
.I x
\-
.I n
*
.IR y ,
for the whole number
.I n
that makes the result have the sign of
.I x
and a magnitude less than that of
.IR y .
fmod(x, 0.0) returns
.IR x .
.PP
All four results are exact.
.SH SEE ALSO
abs(3), frexp(3), intro(3)
.SH HISTORY
The
.B floor
and
.B fmod
functions first appeared in Version 5 AT&T UNIX, and
.B fabs
in Version 6. Version 7 has
.B ceil
as well.
